### 2. Permissions granted / What you MAY do

Without a separate written agreement you may:

1. **View and read** any part of this repository;
2. **Clone and fork** the repository for private, non-commercial academic study;
3. **Run** the code (Julia / Python / multi-language suites) locally for
   scholarly verification and reproducibility checks;
4. **Cite** the work and quote short excerpts (with full attribution to the
   Author and a link to this repository and the DOI
   [10.5281/zenodo.21825394](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21825394));
5. **Reference** figures or results in academic texts, provided the source is
   credited and the citation includes the DOI.

### 3. Restrictions / What you MAY NOT do

Unless explicitly agreed in writing by the Author, you may **not**:

1. Redistribute, republish or mirror substantial parts of the content
   (monographs, full verification tables, figure collections) — in source or
   derived form, including on other forges, preprint servers or archives;
2. Use the content commercially, or include it in paid products, courses or
   services;
3. Present modified versions as your own work, remove or alter attribution,
   copyright notices, DOI references or this licence text;
4. Use the Author's name, ORCID or imagery to endorse derivative works.

### 4. Third-party data / Third-party data

Zeta-zero datasets included under `verification/data/` are compiled from
publicly available tables (A. Odlyzko and others) and remain governed by the
terms of their original sources; the Author claims no ownership over the
underlying zero values.

